It's Portal 2, but:
- without GLaDOS;
- without portal gun;
+ with better soundtrack (10/10, great work);
+ with paint gun and infinite resource of blue and orange gels.
25 chambers (from very easy to above average - there are a few places to stuck) with some fresh ideas. And one terrific run from destructing reactor that makes your fingers cry (took dozens of reloads for me while being a little drunk :D).

Completion time: ~12 hours.
I believe this game is worth the full price. The story is beautiful, as a massive fan of the Borderlands series this is an amazing  lore-heavy installment while we wait for Borderlands 3. There are some massive things happening in the story which will affect later Borderlands games.
I really wonder what would have happened if I picked some of the other choices, as they really seem to matter. So I might even replay this game in the future.
Artstyle: Borderlands 9/10;
Story: Questionable ending 8/10;
Gameplay: Not for everyone 8/10;
Humor: Borderlands 10/10;
Music: Great 8/10;
Voice acting: Amazing 9/10.

